{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/905418-size-suggestion-for-a-location-spirit","id":905418,"title":"Size suggestion for a Location Spirit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-01T23:05:55-07:00","id":905418,"title":"Size suggestion for a Location Spirit","content":"Hello everyone! I am currently in the process of creating a Location Spirit antagonist and I need some help determining the Size (which will factor into its Corpus rating).<br /> <br /> This particular Location Spirit (a Rank 4/Greater Jaggling) is the &quot;Spirit of Portland, Maine&quot; and it is tied to the city itself. So yeah, that's a rather large area! <br /> <br /> The &quot;Book of Spirits&quot; only gives its largest example of a Location Spirit at Size 40 (&quot;Steed's Pond: The Water Horse Pool&quot;) which is tied to small pond.<br /> <br /> So, does anyone have any size suggestions? Maybe a way to convert one mile into a Size Rating and then figure it out based on a city's square miles?<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I guess figuring it out isn't too important, as it's so big that the chances of the PCs actually destroying it are non-existant (but I'm still a bit curious as to how large it would actually be!).<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> - Eric","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5749-starkadder13","name":"Starkadder13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T23:23:38-07:00","id":905426,"title":"","content":"For practicality's sake you'd be better served statting an avatar-shape rather than trying to pin down the Size rating of an entire city \u2014 skyscrapers and shopping malls alone are about Size 100 by the reckoning of the &quot;Destroying a Building&quot; sidebar in Werewolf: Territories, and the spirit of Lonesome Forest from Night Horrors: Wolfsbane has a form small enough to be discretely visible despite looking &quot;like a town would look if it had legs and teeth.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whales and elephants are about Size 15 and 30, respectively, if that's any help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T23:53:44-07:00","id":905435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/905418-size-suggestion-for-a-location-spirit?p=905426#post905426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For practicality's sake you'd be better served statting an avatar-shape rather than trying to pin down the Size rating of an entire city \u2014 skyscrapers and shopping malls alone are about Size 100 by the reckoning of the &quot;Destroying a Building&quot; sidebar in Werewolf: Territories, and the spirit of Lonesome Forest from Night Horrors: Wolfsbane has a form small enough to be discretely visible despite looking &quot;like a town would look if it had legs and teeth.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. &quot;Book of Spirits&quot; suggests that Location Spirits can appear in a form that is humanoid (the spirit of Hollywood Boulevard is given as an example, and she takes the form of a prostitute that walks the length of the boulevard). I am definitely going to go with an avatar-shape as far as visually describing its appearance. A spirit's actual Size though is based (again, according to Book of Spirits) on the Size of the object that spawned it. In this case it is the land itself (the peninsula that Portland would later be built upon) that originally spawned it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5749-starkadder13","name":"Starkadder13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:35:54-07:00","id":905500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starkadder13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/905418-size-suggestion-for-a-location-spirit?p=905435#post905435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes. &quot;Book of Spirits&quot; suggests that Location Spirits can appear in a form that is humanoid (the spirit of Hollywood Boulevard is given as an example, and she takes the form of a prostitute that walks the length of the boulevard). I am definitely going to go with an avatar-shape as far as visually describing its appearance. A spirit's actual Size though is based (again, according to Book of Spirits) on the Size of the object that spawned it. In this case it is the land itself (the peninsula that Portland would later be built upon) that originally spawned it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Subdivide it. A city is a group of places, and the reigning city spirit can be simply the most influential one of those.<br /> <br /> Spirits of whole peninsulas seldom rouse, and when they do, disaster usually follows. Katrina-like disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:54:41-07:00","id":905592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/905418-size-suggestion-for-a-location-spirit?p=905500#post905500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Subdivide it. A city is a group of places, and the reigning city spirit can be simply the most influential one of those.<br /> <br /> Spirits of whole peninsulas seldom rouse, and when they do, disaster usually follows. Katrina-like disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That may be the best way for me to run it. Technically though, as far as the plot of this story arc, a &quot;disaster&quot; of sorts is about to occur.<br /> <br /> This Spirit is for a Victorian Era Geist chronicle I am currently running (the PCs are a Krewe of Sin-Eaters residing in Portland, Maine). Not sure if you are familiar with it, but I am dropping in the story of &quot;The Statue of Weeping Alice&quot; from the &quot;Mysterious Places&quot; supplement book. The backstory for it is left purposely vague (so that Storytellers can tailor it to fit into whatever game line they are running). Basically there is a &quot;curse&quot; that arises from the land itself that forms into an entity surrounding the legend of a little girl named Alice and a statue built in her honor in the center of town. This entity is one that demands sacrifice from the residents of the town or city. When it is worshipped and appeased with offerings (left at the base of the statue), the city prospers. When it is ignored or forgotten the city falls into despair and ruin. When I read it, I immediately thought that making this entity a Location Spirit made the most sense as an explanation to what is actually occurring.<br /> <br /> Since this is a Geist game though, I will be tailoring the story towards the Sin-Eaters as much as I can. Once the mortal residents of the city are driven into fanaticism by the Spirit, they start making human and children sacrifices. Since these are done by the manipulation of this Spirit, these deaths are considered to be &quot;unnatural&quot; by the Laws of Death and the Underworld, skewing the balance between the Living and the Dead. The PCs krewe Channel is all about maintaining that balance, so it will create conflict that they will have to somehow deal with. These deaths will also create more ghosts with unresolved anchors for them to deal with. Since I don't (yet anyway) plan to introduce any werewolf or mage NPCs to help the krewe, their access to entering the Shadow Realm will be slim to none. They will have to ether combat the spirit when its in a state of Twilight (suicidal on their part) or resort to Abjurations or Exorcisms.<br /> <br /> Taking your advice to subdivide the city area, I can attach this Location Spirit to an area of the city (perhaps the known to the locals as the &quot;heart of the city&quot;) where the statue of Alice resides. I can give this area a size of about 70 or so. Since the girl Alice was the biggest sacrifice made (back in the late 1600s), I will have the spirit take on her appearance as an avatar-shape.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your advice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5749-starkadder13","name":"Starkadder13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:34:44-07:00","id":905619,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, make the spirit as big as the statue. Since the protagonists do not have an easy access to confront the spirit directly, having it be of gargantuan size kinda adds insult to injury should they be clever enough to find their way to it.<br /> <br /> The way influence works means a city spirit doesn't have to be the literal biggest fish in the pond, but the one that exerts the biggest pull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}